  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC/DDG COMMUNITY DRIVEN RECOVERY &amp; SAFETY - DRC/DDG CDRD CS</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">DRC/DDG COMMUNITY DRIVEN RECOVERY &amp; SAFETY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC/ DDG has applied to Sida for funding of 45 million SEK to carry out the &quot; Community-Driven Recovery and Safety Programme in Somalia&apos;&apos; during the period 1 November 2014 to 31 December 2016. 

The intervention aims at contributing to the stabilization of fragile parts of Somalia by strengthening social justice through improved community level governance mechanisms and enhancing access to employment opportunities, social services and security for conflict affected populations.

The implementation of the CDRS programme will be done through five different processes:
i) Community Block grants and Social Services Access Grants
ii) Community safety related activities (delivered by DDG under its Community Safety programme)
iii) Conflict prevention and management activities
iv) Livelihood interventions.

The intervention will focus ob two &apos;regions&apos; and a subsequent number of districts in Somalia. Pre-CDRS will be implemented in Warsheikh distrit in Middle Shabelle region followed by CDRS in 20 communities. CDRS will target 40 communities in the Bay/Bakol/Gedo region. Out of these, 20 communities will be in Luug district, Gedo region and the remaining 20 communities will be in Baidoa, Bay Bakol region.

DRC/DDG will implement the CDRS programme alongside the Community Project Implementation Units (CPIUs) from the targeted communities. 

The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is 45 million SEK, all of which will be funded by Sida.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att stabilisera utsatta delar av Somalia d&#xe4;r st&#xe4;rkt social r&#xe4;ttvisa st&#xf6;ds genom att st&#xe4;rka lokalsamh&#xe4;llens styrelse och administration och st&#xf6;d till jobbskapande, f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad samh&#xe4;llsservice och &#xf6;kad s&#xe4;kerhet f&#xf6;r lokalbefolkningen.
CDRS-programmet implementeras genom de f&#xf6;ljande fem komponenterna: 
i)Bidrag till lokalsamh&#xe4;llen f&#xf6;r infrastrukturprojekt
ii)Bidrag f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till samh&#xe4;llstj&#xe4;nster
iii)S&#xe4;kerhetsrelaterade aktiviteter (implementerat av DDG)
iv)F&#xf6;rebyggande och hantering av konflikter
v)Jobbskapande insatser
Programmet fokuserar p&#xe5; tre regioner i Somalia, d&#xe4;r totalt 60 &#x201d;lokalsamh&#xe4;llen&#x201d; (communities) st&#xf6;ds i tre distrikt. I Warsheikh, Mellersta Shabelle, kommer DRC/DDG att implementera en pre-CDRS f&#xf6;ljt av det ullfj&#xe4;drade programmet i 20 lokalsamh&#xe4;llen. I Luug, Gedo-regionen, och i Baidoa, Bay-regionen, st&#xf6;djer programmet 20 lokalsamh&#xe4;llen i vardera distriktet.</narrative>
  </description>
